\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Stupendous height of heavenly love,
\par Of pitying tenderness divine;
\par It brought the Saviour from above,
\par It caused the springing day to shine
\par The sun of righteousness to appear,
\par And gild our gloomy hemisphere.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. God did in Christ Himself reveal,
\par To chase our darkness by His light,
\par Our sin and ignorance dispel,
\par Direct our wandering feet aright;
\par And bring our souls, with pardon blest,
\par To realms of everlasting rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Come then, O Lord, Thy light impart,
\par The faith that bids our terrors cease;
\par Into Thy love direct our heart, 
\par Into Thy way of perfect peace;
\par And cheer the souls of death afraid,
\par And guide them through the dreadful shade
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Answer Thy mercy's whole design,
\par My God incarnated for me;
\par My spirit make Thy radiant shrine,
\par My light and full salvation be;
\par And through the shades of death unknown
\par Conduct me to Thy dazzling throne.
\par                                      Amen\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

